Wait - if `noise_shaping == NOISE_SHAPING_NONE` (0), then `do_dithering` is `false`, and in `dither_output_`, the `if(do_dithering)` branch is skipped, so `LastRandomNumber` is never read. Let me re-read:

```c
static int64_t dither_output_(DitherContext *d, FLAC__bool do_dithering, int shapingtype, int i, double Sum, int k)
{
        double Sum2;
        int64_t val;

        if(do_dithering) {
                if(shapingtype == 0) {
                        double  tmp = random_equi_(d->Dither);
                        Sum2 = tmp - d->LastRandomNumber [k];  // <-- reads uninitialized!
                        d->LastRandomNumber [k] = (int)tmp;
                        Sum2 = Sum += Sum2;
                        val = ROUND64(d, Sum2) & d->Mask;
                }
                ...
        }

        return ROUND64(d, Sum);
}
```

So `LastRandomNumber` is only read when `do_dithering` is true AND `shapingtype == 0`. But `do_dithering` is passed as `noise_shaping != NOISE_SHAPING_NONE`. So if `shapingtype == 0`, then `do_dithering` would be `false`, and the `if(do_dithering)` branch would be skipped. So `LastRandomNumber` would never be read when `shapingtype == 0`.

Hmm, that means the `LastRandomNumber` uninitialized read can't happen through this path. Let me reconsider.

